updated Tue 6 Oct 2026 at 10:11pmTue 6 Oct 2026 at 10:11pmTue 6 Oct 2026 at 10:11pmThe winners of the Nobel Prize in Physics are selected by the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences. (TT News Agency via AP: Christine Olsson)In short:Belgian physicist Francis Halzen has won the Nobel Prize in Physics.The prize was awarded for his work on subatomic particles at the South Pole.What's next?This is Nobel week, with prizes for chemistry and literature to be handed out over the coming days, with the peace prize announced on Friday, local time.abc.net.au/news/francis-halzen-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-physics/107236382Link copiedShareShare articleFrancis Halzen has won the Nobel Prize in Physics for his contributions to the IceCube Neutrino Observatory at the South Pole and his discovery of high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin.Born in Belgium, the 82-year-old scientist is affiliated with the University of Wisconsin–Madison in the US.\"This year's prize is about ghostly messengers from space,\" Ellen Moons, secretary general of the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences, told a news conference, on Tuesday morning, local time.The Academy noted that Professor Halzen's \"vision and scientific leadership\" had been fundamental for the observatory, which it described as \"a cubic kilometre of ice that is equipped with light sensors\".Using the observatory, researchers can capture neutrinos — rare subatomic particles — \"from extremely energy-rich processes in the distant universe\".Trio win Nobel medicine prize for brain activity researchThe prize went to scientists working on the mechanisms the brain uses to switch the activity of individual nerve cells on or off.\"This Nobel Prize is about a giant ice cube positioned at the South Pole of our globe. The ice cube enables the detection of neutrinos,\" Professor Eva Olsson, a member of the Nobel Committee for Physics, told reporters.The prize money this year is 12 million Swedish kronor, ($1.718 million), whether for an individual, a small group of laureates, or an organisation.\"It was a great surprise, and I obviously didn't expect it,\" Professor Halzen told the news conference by telephone shortly after the prize was announced.\"But it's a great pleasure to hear about this prize.\"Last year, three scientists won the Nobel Prize in Physics for research on the strange behaviour of subatomic particles called quantum tunnelling that enabled the ultra-sensitive measurements achieved by MRI machines and laid the groundwork for better cellphones and faster computers.The announcements of this year's prizes began Monday, local time, with the Nobel Prize in Medicine being awarded to three scientists whose work led to a tool that uses light to help unravel how the brain works.This week, the awards for chemistry and literature will also be handed out.The perhaps most keenly anticipated award — the Nobel Peace Prize — is due to be announced on Friday, local time.AP/AFPShare optionsCopy linkFacebookX (formerly Twitter)See more ABC coverage in your search resultsMake ABC a preferred source in GooglePromotionTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerRelated storiesNobel medicine prize awarded to scientists for brain activity researchTopic:Awards and PrizesNobel Peace Prize won't go to Trump this year, experts sayTopic:ExplainerRelated topicsAustraliaAwards and PrizesBelgiumDenmarkEnglandEuropean UnionGermanyPhysicsRussian FederationUnited KingdomUnited StatesTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerJust InFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmAmbulance ramping data casts doubt over LNP promise to reduce wait timesTopic:Ambulance ServiceFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmThe fruit and vegetables to look out for this monthTopic:Food and DrinkFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmMore Just InBack to top","title":"Nobel Prize in Physics honours work on 'ghost messengers from space'","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-06/francis-halzen-wins-2026-nobel-prize-in-physics/107236382","id":218},{"content_hash":"b4aa05fdab058512fad567d97c0e46ababff1762ae74edcba3341a75e13a3a16","domain":"ml.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:29:20.883767+00:00","final_url":"https://www.ml.com/articles/awards-recognition.html","language":"","text":"Our top advisors. Your top goals. Merrill advisors are recognized for excellence and relentlessly focused on helping you achieve your unique financial goals. Explore our latest awards FORBES 2026 Top Next-Gen Wealth Advisors Published on August 11, 2026. Rankings based on data as of March 31, 2026. 31 Merrill advisors FORBES 2026 Best-in-State Next-Gen Wealth Advisors Published on August 11, 2026. Rankings based on data as of March 31, 2026. 446 Merrill advisors 17 Merrill advisors ranked #1 in state/region BARRON'S 2026 Top 100 Women Financial Advisors Published on July 17