aturn Says Finish What You Promised at Work; Uttara Phalguni Moon Turns Focus Homeward2027 LPGA season opener gets star-studded concert lineup with John Fogerty and Brooks & DunnBrittany Mahomes vs. Randi Mahomes? Patrick Mahomes’ mom eyes Chiefs fashion spaceJammu & Kashmir: Landmine found along LoC in Poonch, destroyedNasa sent tiny glow-in-the-dark squid to the space station; scientists removed gravity to study how their glowing bacteria colonise and influence themWWE Money in the Bank 2026: What time does it start in US, UK and India, where to watch on Netflix and ESPN, Roman Reigns vs LA Knight and full cardCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved. For reprint rights: Times Syndication ServiceFollow Us On","title":"Country singer Zach Bryan quietly bought an $18 million Tennessee estate in 2026; the secluded property sits on 146 acres and includes a 6,000-square-foot main house and recording studio","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/country-singer-zach-bryan-quietly-bought-an-18-million-tennessee-estate-in-2026-the-secluded-property-sits-on-146-acres-and-includes-a-6000-square-foot-main-house-and-recording-studio/articleshow/134779303.cms","id":289},{"content_hash":"f504f83ad30076dec733394594dd9005797590d597f61692e553f5eea9e8afa7","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:29:04.536150+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/topic/local-government","language":"","text":"Local Government - Topic - ABC NewsSkip to main contentSkip to news navigation, settings and searchExplore the ABC More from ABCClose menuABC ABC News ABC iview ABC listen Kids & Students Indigenous Information & ServicesEditorial PoliciesRead our editorial guiding principlesFollow the ABCnewsiviewlistenLoadingABC NewsJust InFor YouPoliticsWorldBusinessAnalysisSportLifestyleEntertainmentQuizzesMoreSearchNews HomeJust InFor YouAnalysisRuralWatch LiveHealthIndigenousPoliticsScienceDeep TimeElectionsWorldEnvironmentInvestigationsBusinessLocal newsQuizzesSportAFLNRLFootballTennisCricketNetballLifestyleWellbeingRelationships & FamilyFood & RecipesPersonal FinanceHome & GardenEntertainmentTV & MoviesBooksMusicPop CultureArtsFacebookYouTubeInstagramTwitterEmergencyBackstoryNewsletters中文新闻BERITA BAHASA INDONESIATOK PISIN Appearance (BETA) Follow system settings Select an optionAlways lightAlways darkFollow system settingsABC iViewABC ListenLocal GovernmentGovernment's 'unusual intervention' in Sydney Town Hall projectTopic:Urban Development and PlanningTopic:Local GovernmentThe council says the plaza, which will require the demolition of several buildings the city has obtained since the 1980s, is necessary to create a gathering point for community events, music events and markets.'Fed a lie': Locals frustrated as construction site remains at famous WA beachTopic:Urban Development and PlanningDeputy mayor candidate could be sacked if suspension is upheldTopic:Local GovernmentSmall SA town's 'out of control' pigeon populationTopic:PestsLogan mayor warns of backyard 'slums' as council slashes granny flat taxTopic:Local GovernmentParents, signs and ageism: Hobart's council race turns ugly as voting beginsAccusations of ageism, fury over sign placement, ongoing debate over town hall snacks, and a fiery confrontation involving a lord mayor hopeful's parents are just some of the incidents to have unfolded.Topic:Local GovernmentWed 7 Oct 2026 at 7:24amWed 7 Oct 2026 at 7:24amWed 7 Oct 2026 at 7:24am'Forgotten' outback town faces scorching summer without a poolThe pool in the western NSW town of Walgett will remain closed this summer, with council finding it was unsafe and beyond repair.Topic:Outdoor Recreational ActivitiesSun 4 Oct 2026 at 9:55amSun 4 Oct 2026 at 9:55amSun 4 Oct 2026 at 9:55amTasmania's top prosecutor rules out 'further action' on town hall snack sagaTasmania's top prosecutor has declined to take action over the taking of snacks from Hobart Town Hall by the city's deputy lord mayor, potentially bringing the contentious saga to a close.Topic:Local GovernmentFri 2 Oct 2026 at 3:39pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 3:39pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 3:39pmBig housing development set to grow Warrnambool's population by 50 per centAn additional 15,000 people could call this Great Ocean Road city home when this development is complete.Topic:Housing PolicyFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:59pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:59pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:59pmAssault charge against Yarra mayor Stephen Jolly dismissedCouncillor Jolly was accused of striking a gatecrasher after she arrived at a 2024 local government election afterparty to protest his victory.Topic:CourtsFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:32pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:32pmFri 2 Oct 2026 at 2:32pm'Information-rich' generation makes voice heard in politicsFrom building a dog park to overhauling Queensland's disaster preparedness, young people are engaging politically with the issues that matter to their communities. While some try out traditional politics, many are turning to newer forms of advocacy.Topic:Young PeopleFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:31amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:31amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:31amBeloved Melbourne market to have 900 apartments under redevelopment planResidential towers ranging in height from eight to 16 storeys would surround the market and include 10 per cent affordable housing under plans to redevelop the site.Topic:Local GovernmentFri 2 Oct 2026 at 10:54amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 10:54amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 10:54amNotorious Tasmanian road could be re-routedA notoriously windy stretch of road in Tasmania could be upgraded with pricing revealed to be as high as $2.7 billion to re-route the road.Topic:InfrastructureFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:42amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:42amFri 2 Oct 2026 at 8:42amMore local council mergers on cards as Claremont votes for amalgamationThe Town of Claremont in Perth's western suburbs is open to exploring merging with another council, with its mayor saying \"it is probably time\" for the move.Topic:Local GovernmentThu 1 Oct 2026 at 5:57pmThu 1 Oct 2026 at 5:57pmThu 1 Oct 2026 at 5:57pmWhale carcass on Perth beach awaits crane big enough to move itA 13-metre-long whale carcass that washed up at City Beach on Monday will remain on the sand overnight, with a crane big enough to lift it expected to arrive on site in the morning.Topic:AnimalsWed 30 Sep 2026 at 9:14pmWed 30 Sep 2026 at 9:14pmWed 30 Sep 2026 at 9:14pmEmergency water restrictions for Queensland town following pump failureClermont residents are still being urged to conserve water, while storage levels are critically low due to multiple pump failures.Topic:Water SupplyWed 30 Sep 2026 at 12:47pmWed 30 Sep 2026 at 12:47pmWed 30 Sep 2026 at 12:47pmCoober Pedy's transition out of administration delayed indefinitelyThe South Australian government's timeline to transition the District Council of Coober Pedy out of administration is set to be discarded — without any new end date being set.Topic:Local GovernmentWed 30 Sep 2026 at 6:02amWed 30 Sep 2026 at 6:02amWed 30 Sep 2026 at 6:02amBrisbane cyclist who lost eye wins $675k negligence payoutVictor George Dennison, who was 64 at the time, lost an eye and was left with a traumatic brain injury after a bicycle crash on a Brisbane footpath in 2009.Topic:CourtsTue 29 Sep 2026 at 4:38pmTue 29 Sep 2026 at 4:38pmTue 29 Sep 2026 at 4:38pmParramatta elects youngest lord mayor after Liberal quits partyCameron MacLean is elected to the position by a single vote, which came from a councillor who left her party on the same morning.Topic:Local GovernmentTue 29 Sep 2026 at 8:28amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 8:28amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 8:28amMelbourne council endorses antisemitism action plan in Victorian firstGlen Eira City Council will become the first council in the state to endorse an antisemitism strategy, following a reported rise from residents in antisemitic incidents.Topic:Religious DiscriminationTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:35amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:35amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:35amMayor defends cocktails, AirPods, steaks, KFC credit card spendA Tasmanian mayor defends items bought with a work-issued credit card that racked up more than $17,000 across three years.Topic:Local GovernmentTue 29 Sep 2026 at 9:54amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 9:54amTue 29 Sep 2026 at 9:54amBrisbane's Story Bridge to close over new year for maintenanceBrisbane's iconic Story Bridge is set to close for three weeks over the new year for maintenance. The repairs include resurfacing the southern approach and parts of the northern approach, as well as structural deck maintenance and waterproofing.Topic:Local GovernmentSun 27 Sep 2026 at 12:34pmSun 27 Sep 2026 at 12:34pmSun 27 Sep 2026 at 12:34pm'Sudden' death of SA woman from falling tree branch preventable, coroner findsSouth Australian school teacher Judith Anne Ditter died in November 2020 when a heavy branch hit a car she was travelling in on an Adelaide Hills road.Topic:Road Accidents and IncidentsThu 24 Sep 2026 at 3:53pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 3:53pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 3:53pm'Distressing': Homeless campers forced to pack up as authorities move inHomeless people living in a makeshift camp in Rockingham are packing up their belongings after being ordered to leave the area by the end of the day. Topic:HomelessnessThu 24 Sep 2026 at 4:25pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 4:25pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 4:25pmIpswich mayor says new council media policy aimed at gagging herIpswich City Council passes amendments to its media policy to allow all councillors to use communications staff to write and send media releases, a move the mayor says is designed minimise her voice.Topic:Local GovernmentThu 24 Sep 2026 at 12:33pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 12:33pmThu 24 Sep 2026 at 12:33pmLoad more stories aboveBack to topABC NewsContact ABC NewsYour home of Australian stories, conversations and events that shape our nation.This service may include material from Agence France-Presse (AFP), APTN, Reuters, AAP, CNN and the BBC World Service which is copyright and cannot be reproduced.Follow ABC NewsSectionsABC News HomeJust InFor YouWatch Live NewsLive AB