olicy Thank you! Your submission has been received!Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. Really Good Emails is part of Beefree. It started as a volunteer project in 2014.©2026 BEE Content Design, Inc. All rights reserved. Terms | Privacy & Cookie Policy | DMCA Cookies Preferences and Your Privacy Choice Can we be honest?We want your email address. Let us send you the best emails designs and links twice a week.Name*Email*I’m okay with getting emails and having that activity tracked to improve my experience, and I agree to the Privacy PolicyThank you! Your submission has been received!Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. DisclaimerWe’ve updated our Privacy Policy. We encourage you to review it here.Legal and Privacy infoReally Good Emails is part of Beefree. It started as a volunteer project in 2014.© 2026 BEE Content Design, Inc. All rights reserved. Terms | Privacy & Cookie Policy | DMCACookies Preferences and Your Privacy Choice","title":"International Women's Day Celebration | Email template - RGE Studio","url":"https://reallygoodemails.com/template/international-womens-day-celebration","id":336},{"content_hash":"3d45c54719bbf1a90bd481993a1003950be1fd4eff421a305b985ae11d48c592","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:54.415797+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/07/le-general-leblanc-remplace-le-general-lorillot-a-hue_2073326_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Cet article vous est offert Pour lire gratuitement cet article réservé aux abonnés, connectez-vous Se connecter Vous n'êtes pas inscrit sur Le Monde ? Inscrivez-vous gratuitement Archives Archives Archives LE GÉNÉRAL LEBLANC remplace le général Lorillot à Hué Le Monde Publié le 07 novembre 1951 à 00h00, modifié le 07 novembre 1951 à 00h00 Article réservé aux abonnés Lire plus tard Mettre Le Monde en favori sur Google Partager Partager sur Messenger Partager sur Facebook Envoyer par e-mail Partager sur Linkedin Copier le lien","title":"LE GÉNÉRAL LEBLANC remplace le général Lorillot à Hué","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/07/le-general-leblanc-remplace-le-general-lorillot-a-hue_2073326_1819218.html","id":337},{"content_hash":"3425ae92d979e0f16c63da0daac015cedf60d63f2f9f59bcb7111b5cefe65b92","domain":"timesofindia.indiatimes.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:54.343641+00:00","final_url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-suspends-8-tech-firms-from-perm-process-full-list-and-what-it-means/articleshow/134804057.cms","language":"","text":"US suspends 8 tech firms from PERM process: Full list and what it means - The Times of IndiaEditionININUSGCCEnglishEnglishहिन्दीमराठीಕನ್ನಡதமிழ்বাংলাമലയാളംతెలుగుગુજરાતીWeatherSign InTOIworldUSTimes EvokePakistanSouth AsiaUKEuropeChinaMiddle East US StreamersRest of WorldMad, Mad WorldVideosToday's ePaperLiveNewsWorld NewsUS NewsUS suspends 8 tech firms from PERM process: Full list and what it meansTrendingChrista PikeZohran MamdaniMarco RubioSaudi Syria RelationsSaudi Arabia Airport AttackDonald TrumpIran War NewsChrista PikeZohran MamdaniMarco RubioSaudi Syria RelationsSaudi Arabia Airport AttackDonald TrumpIran War NewsChrista PikeZohran MamdaniMarco RubioSaudi Syria RelationsSaudi Arabia Airport AttackDonald TrumpIran War NewsUS suspends 8 tech firms from PERM process: Full list and what it meansEdited by: Ayush Pandey / TIMESOFINDIA.COM / Updated: Oct 09, 2026, 08:28 ISTSaveCommentsShareAa+Text SizeSmallMediumLargePrint US President Donald Trump. The US administration has suspended eight major technology companies from the employment-based green card process, leaving thousands of foreign professionals, including Indian IT workers, facing uncertainty over their permanent residency plans.The companies named in the October 8 order are Microsoft, Adobe, Cognizant, Infosys, Tata Consultancy Services (TCS), Wipro, HCL Technologies and Capgemini. The US Department of Labor said it would neither accept new Permanent Labor Certification (PERM) applications involving these firms nor process pending ones.The administration has cited alleged abuse of employment-based immigration programmes and the need to protect American workers. US Vice President JD Vance accused Microsoft of laying off American workers while seeking H-1B approvals and green cards for foreign employees. Cognizant had also faced a suspension of its US green card filings in September amid a probe into possible visa fraud.PERM is a key step in obtaining many employer-sponsored green cards. It requires employers to demonstrate that there are not enough qualified, willing and available American workers for a position and that hiring a foreign worker will not adversely affect wages and working conditions.The suspension does not automatically cancel existing H-1B visas or green cards. However, employees with pending PERM applications could face delays, while those whose employers have not yet filed applications may be unable to begin the usual process through these companies. Workers whose PERM certifications have already been approved are in a different position, as the order does not automatically invalidate existing approvals.The decision could create additional uncertainty for H-1B workers approaching the standard six-year limit, particularly those relying on their green card process to qualify for extensions. Some employees may explore sponsorship through another employer, but applications do not automatically transfer when workers change jobs.The duration of the suspension remains uncertain. JD Vance said it would continue “as long as it needs to”. The affected companies could also challenge the decision in federal court. The impact on individual workers will depend on the status of their immigration cases and the length of the suspension.You use AI every day. Now get your AI Quotient. Take the AIQ test.About the AuthorAyush PandeyAyush Pandey is a journalist at The Times of India, covering breaking news, politics, defence, and major legal and policy developments across India and the world. His reporting focuses on elections, national security, and institutional affairs, tracking the decisions and conflicts that shape public life. He specialises in sharp explainers and in-depth feature stories that go beyond headlines to decode political shifts, defence strategy, geopolitical flashpoints, and changing public sentiment. His work combines speed, clarity, and depth for a fast-moving digital audience.Read MoreEnd of ArticleFollow Us On Social MediaVideosExplosions Rock Iraqi Kurdistan; Iran's Shahed-136 Drone Blitz Targets Kurdish Separatists In ErbilChina Russia Could Hit U.S_ Hegseth Faces Nuclear Reality On Cam; Iran War EXPOSES Trump _ Watch‘Trump's Reckless War!’: Hakeem Jeffries Blasts Hegseth Amid LA-San Diego 'Bombing' RowON CAM: Saudi Jet BLOWN TO PIECES! First Images Emerge After Houthis Strike Riyadh Airport‘Rusty, Battered & Broken!’: USS Lincoln ‘Scarred’ By Iran War; New Visuals Shock Families | WatchTrump Readies MASSIVE Iran Attack? Pentagon Prepares For Strikes On Nuclear SitesNidal Hasan Execution: Pete Hegseth Orders Ford Hood Shooter's 'Firing Squad' Live Streaming‘Why The Silence On Oct 7?’: Abdul El-Sayed Walks Away From Reporter; Then Rips Trump‘Not Playing This Game’: Marco Rubio Unloads On Reporter Over Kimberly Guilfoyle’s $100,000 BribeZohran Mamdani Grilled Over Oct. 7 Post; Reporter Asks: ‘Will You Apologize To Netanyahu?’123Photostories5 things couples secretly stop doing before they break upQuote of the day: “Love looks not with the eyes, but with the mind”; William Shakespeare’s timeless words on how true love goes beyond what we seeGender pain gap: Women experience more pain than men across the whole body, major global study finds ‘shocking’ dataFrom historic tiaras to priceless heirlooms: The royal jewels Kate Middleton has left untouchedKangana Ranaut goes full Himachali royalty in a statement topi, Kullu shawl, and a cultural nod to President Droupadi 