lowing Yourself to Feel Peace - The Times of IndiaEditionININUSGCCEnglishEnglishहिन्दीमराठीಕನ್ನಡதமிழ்বাংলাമലയാളംతెలుగుગુજરાતીWeatherSign InTOIAstrologyHoroscopeSun Sign PredictionsCompatibility CalculatorYearly Horoscope 2026Chinese HoroscopeNumerologyNumerology PredictionsPlanets TransitsGemstones Vastu & feng shuikundali dasha & RemediesReligionMonthly HoroscopeOthersToday's ePaperLiveNewsAstrology NewsHoroscope NewsBuddhist Quote Of The Day, October 9, 2026: Stop Waiting for Life to Become Perfect Before Allowing Yourself to Feel PeaceTrendingHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayBuddhist Quote Of The Day, October 9, 2026: Stop Waiting for Life to Become Perfect Before Allowing Yourself to Feel PeaceTOI Astrology / Oct 09, 2026, 04:20 ISTSaveCommentsShareAa+Text SizeSmallMediumLargePrint People frequently await the ideal conditions to attain serenity, yet these conditions may never arise. Astrology implies that today offers a chance to balance life’s pressures, particularly with the Sun's alignment in Libra. It’s possible to achieve a state of tranquility even with ongoing issues, aided by retrograde effects. Simple self-care routines and taking time off can foster this inner peace. Many people keep a private list of conditions. The workload must ease, the family must settle, the bank balance must grow. Only then will calm be allowed in. But that day keeps moving further off, and Friday arrives with the list still unfinished.The zodiac gives a useful marker today. The Sun is in Libra, ruled by Venus and tied to harmony, so the search for steadiness between competing demands is easy to notice.Buddhist Quote of the Day: Dhammapada 202The verse names lust, hatred and the restless clinging of the mind as the great fires. No happiness, it says, ranks higher than peace. Translators choose slightly different words.Peace is not described as a reward for tidy circumstances. It is treated as something the mind can reach while the fires are being put out.The Perfect Moment Never ArrivesA delayed refund, a difficult colleague and a cluttered house will all still be there next month. Some problems get solved and new ones take their place. Waiting for a clear run is waiting for something that rarely happens.Neptune is retrograde in Aries, which lends a glow to imagined futures. The picture of a flawless life looks convincing from a distance. Compare it with the ordinary week actually in front of you.Peace Sits Beside the ProblemsCalm does not require every issue to be closed. A person can carry an unpaid bill and still take a slow breath. Both facts exist together.Saturn, retrograde in Aries, keeps unfinished matters visible. That is uncomfortable, yet it also removes the pretence. Handle what can be handled today. Leave the remainder without guilt.Allow Small Rest NowJupiter in Leo supports generous self-treatment. Take a proper lunch break. Walk to the shop without the phone. These acts are modest, but they show the body that rest is permitted before the workload ends.Pluto is retrograde in Aquarius, where long-standing group pressures are slowly reviewed. You can question expectations others place on you. You do not owe anyone a constant show of busyness.Peace as a Present PracticeThe Buddhist lesson for October 9 is that stillness belongs to this hour, not to some improved future. Each time the mind drops the demand for perfection, a little calm follows.Before the evening, choose ten minutes with no task attached. Sit, breathe and let the unfinished list stay unfinished. The New Moon in Libra arrives tomorrow, a fitting moment to start this habit.Get the latest astrology news and horoscope updates. Download the 